# Crystal Imperium play test: boot -> new game -> settings -> Falkner (trainer 402).
# Team: Cyndaquil / Mareep / Geodude at the pre-Falkner level cap (15), given via the debug menu.
# Passes when the battle against the real AI and party data runs to a result.

# Title screen and Oak's intro (name entry is filled by mashing A)
wait 1300
press START
wait 60
press A
wait 500
mash A 900
mash A 900
shot 01_settings_intro.png
# Challenge menu: confirm defaults (Minimal Grinding ON) from the Challenges tab
mash A 700
shot 02_challenge_menu.png
press R
wait 20
press R
wait 20
press R
wait 20
press R
wait 20
press R
wait 30
press UP
wait 30
press A
wait 120
press A
wait 120
mash A 1500
mash A 1200
wait 300
shot 03_overworld.png

# Battle Style SET, so the autopilot is never asked "Will you switch?"
!battle_style_set()

# Team at the level cap
!give_mon(155, 15)
!give_mon(179, 15)
!give_mon(74, 15)
expect8 {gPlayerPartyCount} 3 party_has_three_mons
# Minimal Grinding: Lv15 Cyndaquil and Geodude with 31 IVs / 0 EVs have exactly 41 max HP (maxHP
# is at offset 88)
expect16 {gPlayerParty+88} 41 cyndaquil_max_hp_31iv_0ev
expect16 {gPlayerParty+288} 41 geodude_max_hp_31iv_0ev

# Falkner
!battle_trainer(402)
wait 300
press A
wait 200
press A
wait 200
press A
wait 220
shot 04_falkner_start.png
expect16 {gBattleMons+136} 16 falkner_leads_pidgey
# The battle is played by the autopilot (it follows the battle state, so it also runs on other
# emulators, whose RNG seed differs): Cyndaquil Ember, Mareep Thunder Shock, Geodude Rollout
# (move slots at level 15: Leer / Ember / Smokescreen / Quick Attack, Thunder Wave / Thunder Shock
# / Cotton Spore / Charge, Mud Sport / Rock Polish / Rollout / Magnitude).
# The hand-played winning line is in docs/crystal_imperium/BALANCE.md.
!autobattle("1,1,2")
shot 07_result.png
peek8 {gBattleOutcome} battle_outcome_1_win_2_loss
expectne8 {gBattleOutcome} 0 battle_ran_to_completion
